<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch PTT buys Sweden Post stake in GD Net.</title>
<headline>Dutch PTT buys Sweden Post stake in GD Net.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch post and telecommunications group Koninklijke PTT NV (KPN) said on Wednesday its unit PTT Post had bought Sweden Post's unit GD Net.</p>
<p>GD Net owns half of GD Express Worldwide. The other half is owned by Australia's TNT Ltd, which was recently taken over by KPN.</p>
<p>GD Express Worldwide is an internationally active express distribution company, which works under the trade name TNT Express Worldwide.</p>
<p>Sweden Post and PTT Post have agreed to continue their present commercial links, the Dutch group said.</p>
<p>No financial details of the transaction were given.</p>
